{"name":"Steam","hex":"#dddddd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steam","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hot gaseous form of water, formed when water changes from the liquid phase to the gas phase (at or above its boiling point temperature).","The suspended condensate (cloud) formed by water vapour when it encounters colder air.\nMist, fog.\nExhaled breath into cold air below the dew point of the exhalation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook with steam.","To be cooked with steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam","wikidata":"Q3251738"},{"title":"Steam (service)","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is a digital distribution platform for PC games by the American video game studio Valve. It was launched as a software client in September 2003 to provide video game updates automatically for Valve's games and expanded to distributing third-party titles in late 2005. Steam offers various features, such as game server matchmaking with Valve Anti-Cheat (VAC) measures, social networking, and game streaming services. The Steam client functions include update maintenance, cloud storage, and community features such as direct messaging, an in-game overlay, discussion forums, and a virtual collectable marketplace. The storefront also offers productivity software, game soundtracks, videos, and sells hardware made by Valve, such as the Valve Index and the Steam Deck."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Steam_%28service%29.png/330px-Steam_%28service%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_(service)","wikidata":"Q337535"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/1280px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling water creating steam in an electric kettle ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoilingkettle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fireless steam locomotive. Despite the resemblance to a boiler, note the lack of a chimney and also how the cylinders are at the cab end, not the chimney end.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Celeste_Steam_page_top.png/500px-Celeste_Steam_page_top.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons